---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../config';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Tally"
  description="Tally collects no data. No account, no analytics, no tracking — your Screen Time data stays on your device."
>
  <Nav />

  <main class="wrap doc" id="main">
    <h1>Tally Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Effective November 15, 2026</p>

    <p>
      Tally helps you set daily time limits on apps you choose. It is designed
      so that your data stays on your device. This policy explains what that
      means.
    </p>

    <h2>Data we collect</h2>
    <p>
      None. Tally has no account system, no analytics, no advertising, and no
      tracking. The app does not send any personal data, usage data, or
      identifiers to us or to any third party.
    </p>

    <h2>Screen Time data</h2>
    <p>
      Tally uses Apple’s Screen Time framework (FamilyControls, DeviceActivity
      and ManagedSettings) with your permission. Through this framework the app
      receives only opaque tokens that stand for the apps, categories and
      websites you select — not their names or your activity inside them. Apple
      processes usage on your device and tells Tally when a limit is reached.
      Usage totals displayed in the app are produced on your device and never
      leave it.
    </p>

    <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Your rules (name, selected app tokens, daily limits), daily usage totals,
      and a history of the extra time you granted yourself are stored locally
      in the app’s private storage, shared only with Tally’s own extensions on
      the same device. Deleting a rule removes its data; deleting the app
      removes everything.
    </p>

    <h2>Notifications</h2>
    <p>
      If you allow notifications, Tally schedules local notifications on your
      device (for example, when you ask for more time from a block screen). No
      push notification service is used.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Tally is intended for people managing their own screen time. It does not
      knowingly collect any information from anyone, including children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page
      with a new effective date.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy:
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
    </p>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .doc {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding-top: 80px;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 40px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .updated {
    color: var(--text-faint);
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-top: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-top: 44px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  p {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  ul {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    padding-left: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--indigo);
  }

  a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
